<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Exp Med</journal-id><journal-title>The Journal of Experimental Medicine</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0022-1007</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-9538</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">19868634</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2128127</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>HEAT AND GROWTH-INHIBITING ACTION OF SERUM</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Carrel</surname><given-names>Alexis</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Ebeling</surname><given-names>Albert H.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="N0x36114c0N0x1d80d78">From the Laboratories of The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research.</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>30</day><month>4</month><year>1922</year></pub-date><volume>35</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>647</fpage><lpage>656</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>4</day><month>1</month><year>1922</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; Copyright, 1922, by The Rockefeller Institute for Medical Research New York</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> The inhibiting action of homologous serum on the proliferation of fibroblasts <italic>in vitro</italic> was increased after the serum had been heated at 56&#x000b0; and 70&#x000b0;C. This action decreased after the serum had been heated at 100&#x000b0;C. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>